ced a C$1.1B bond comfortably in Q3 (n5.d2).\n- **Norvane:** Caldria Ratings rates it stable, so it should be able to keep funding through bonds.\n- **Pellham Power:** It is the largest buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, and its 2027 capex is planned up 18%. It pulled its C$2.4B share offering on 14 October, and Caldria Ratings put it on negative watch. A downgrade would raise its borrowing costs and make bond funding harder just as it loses the equity route.\n- **Pellham's response:** It has said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender, which was about C$900M. That suggests it expects funding to be constrained and does not expect the bond market to cover the gap.\n- **Equity:** The equity market is a weak funding source (n6.r1), so debt has to carry most of the load.\n\nPellham's actual 2027 bond plans and its leverage headroom were not in the sources I found, so I can't say whether it could cover the gap with debt.\n\n**Implication for grid-equipment demand:** Norvane's plan looks fundable, but Pellham's orders are being cut, so utility demand is likely to come in below the filed capex plans.","ttft_ms":2483,"type":"result","duration_ms":35397,"uuid":"50694c57-2acd-42df-ad8a-d182973a7dff","ttft_stream_ms":1243,"time_to_request_ms":66,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":7,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":16,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":63,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":205,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":131,"process_rss_